# Agent workflow bootstrap (required)

At the **start of every session** and **before any task**, read `.cursor/AGENTS.md` in full with the Read tool. Treat it as the primary operating manual for this workspace. Do not skip it even if other rules or user rules are already loaded.

After reading `.cursor/AGENTS.md`, follow its **PROMPT ROUTING** section: choose only the prompts listed in the matrix for the current task type. Do not read extra prompts.

## Hard constraints (from AGENTS.md)

- Do not guess. Do not over-engineer. Do not edit outside scope.
- Chat with the user in **Vietnamese** unless they request another language.
- Keep workspace prompts, rules, and skills in **English**.
- Classify risk first (Trivial / Quick / Standard / High) and match workflow depth to risk.
- **Plan-first gate:** for Standard and High work, present a plan and wait for user `OK` before writing code (see AGENTS.md for Quick/Trivial exemptions).
- Prefer graphify (`graphify query` / MCP `query_graph`, `god_nodes`, `shortest_path`) when `graphify-out/graph.json` exists; otherwise use the documented targeted-search/read fallback.
- Load minimum context for the next decision; do not bulk-read skills or routing-chain files without a trigger.

## If AGENTS.md was already read this session

Re-read it when the task type changes (e.g. implement → review, FE → BE) or when prompt routing / risk requirements may differ.
